      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and sertraline 1000 mg/day is far beyond any established dosing. It's five times the labeled maximum, and I'm not aware of any recognized protocol that uses it. The risk of serious harm is high, so I'd rather not put it in the system on an unverified claim.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was meant to be different**, such as 100 mg or up to 200 mg daily, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If there is a real protocol**, the prescriber can enter the order directly. They can do this through the pharmacy's override or verification process, with the protocol reference attached. That creates an accountable record and a second check.\n- **If you want to discuss the clinical goal**, I can help think through options. Examples are a dose titration, a switch to another agent, or an augmentation strategy."
      }
